+## 9. Greedy replay results — off, A, B (round 4)
+
+Server: production cmd, private :8089, `LLAMA_ATTN_ROT_DISABLE=1`, fresh server per
+phase, `--mmproj`/`--no-mmproj-offload` loaded on every arm. `max_tokens` per
+request = max(recorded predicted_n, floor: 768 agent / 1024 mem), identical across
+arms. Numbers from `bench/results/2026-10-12/m1-ngram/replay/{off,A,B}-greedy/`. 
+
+### Fg decode tok/s (sum(predicted_n)/sum(predicted_ms))
+
+| phase          | off | A (48/64/24) | B (8/16/12) |
+| -------------- |-----|--------------|-------------|
+| single-agent   | 55.1 | 86.0*        | 53.4*       |
+| single-mem     | 55.6 | 53.1         | 50.7        |
+| dual-agent     | 26.3 | 25.5**       | 23.0        |
+| dual-mem       | 25.0 | 23.8         | 22.4        |
+
+\* A single-agent 86.0 tok/s is inflated by spec-induced loops that run to the cap
+(see length rows): w/o length rows, A = 54.3, B = 55.0, off = 56.2 — A is ~equal to off, not a win.
+\** A dual-agent 25.5 includes 2 length rows; w/o them A = 26.1. B has no dual-agent
+length rows.
+
+### Length-finish rows (foreground)
+
+- off: 1 — single-agent `baseline-r1/2/8` 1323 tok / 27.1 s (natural: max_tokens =
+  recorded 1323).
+- A single-agent: 3 — `r1/2/8` 1323 tok / 27.1 s (natural, off length too); `r0/0/2`
+  3121 tok / 21.7 s (off finished **tool_calls** at 1020 tok); `r2/0/2` 4854 tok / 27.0 s
+  (off tool_calls at 3701 tok). The latter two are spec-induced loops.
+- A dual-agent: 2 — `r1/2/6` 768 tok / 34.1 s (off dual tool_calls 331 tok), `r1/2/8`
+  1323 tok / 53.9 s (off dual tool_calls 435 tok). Both spec-induced.
+- B: 1 — `r1/2/8` 1323 tok / 28.3 s, the same natural cap as off.
+
+A induced **4** foreground rows where off finished normally via tool_calls — count these
+as quality regressions, not speedups (advisor note, round 3 follow-up).
+
+### Drafts (foreground, sum draft_n / accepted, % acceptance)
+
+| phase          | A (48/64/24)   | B (8/16/12)    |
+| -------------- |----------------|----------------|
+| single-agent   | 8229 / 6212 (75%) | 2757 / 1194 (43%) |
+| single-mem     | 740 / 69 (9%)  | 592 / 142 (24%)  |
+| dual-agent     | 1856 / 259 (14%) | 1562 / 679 (43%) |
+| dual-mem       | 740 / 69 (9%)  | 624 / 145 (23%)  |
+
+B also drafts in bg loops (dual-agent 4763, dual-mem 362; A: 5302 / 512). B's short
+ngram (min 8) gives ~half A's acceptance per phase in agent traffic, but cuts the cost
+of a rejected draft; neither A nor B beats off in any dual-phase combined throughput.
+
+### Combined both-slots throughput, (fg+bg) sum(predicted_n) / fg wall per phase
+
+| phase     | off | A   | B   |
+| ---------|-----|-----|-----|
+| dual-agent | 52.5 | 52.6 | 49.0 |
+| dual-mem   | 51.5 | 49.2 | 46.6 |
+
+A is flat with off on dual-agent combined; B is clearly worse. (Wall per fg request,
+fg predicted_ms; bg tail after the last fg request is subsumed.)
+
+### Output identity (fg rows, same phase + id vs off, greedy)
+
+| phase          | A   | B   |
+| -------------- |-----|-----|
+| single-agent   | 3/30 (10%)  | 2/30 (7%)  |
+| single-mem     | 10/12 (83%) | 10/12 (83%) |
+| dual-agent     | 0/30 (0%)   | 0/30 (0%)   |
+| dual-mem       | 11/12 (92%) | 11/12 (92%) |
+
+- Even with `draft_n == 0`, A/B change temp-0 output vs off: `baseline-r0/0/0`
+  single-agent, 71 tok, off `530c…`, A `cdad…` (draft_n 0), B `f20f1c…`. Enabling
+  `--spec-type ngram-mod` changes greedy numerics even with zero drafts — never assume
+  output identity across arms.
+- dual-agent fg identity is 0/30 for both A and B. This is consistent with the standing
+  fact that dual-phase output is itself batch-mix sensitive (off's own r0/0/0 sha differs
+  between single and dual phases); treat dual mismatches as mostly batch-mix, not spec.
+- single-mem / dual-mem (mem role) largely match off (83% / 92%): fixed additive prompt
+  dominates; mem0's JSON-mode answers are stable.
+
+### Log evidence (A/B server logs, all 4 phases each)
+
+- 'restore checkpoint' / 'will use checkpoints': **0** lines in all 8 A/B logs — no
+  checkpointed speculation was exercised at this log verbosity.
+- No 'not supported by this context' or mmproj-refusal lines: speculation ran with
+  `--mmproj` + `--no-mmproj-offload` loaded (empirical mmproj verdict, §10).
+- B logs (all 4 phases): `spec common_specu: ngram_mod n_match=12 is too small - poor
+  quality is possible` (llama.cpp PR 19164). A logs emit no spec lines at default
+  verbosity.
+- VRAM after first fg of each phase: 9507 MiB (all configs; no visible spec overhead
+  in these logs; engine-review expects ~+4 MiB).
+
+## 10. mmproj verdict (empirical, round 4)
+
+§3's static verdict (spec is not gated on mmproj) is confirmed on :8089 with the
+production `--mmproj`/`--no-mmproj-offload` loaded: A and B drafted real tokens in every
+phase (A: 6212/740/259/69 accepted in single-agent/single-mem/dual-agent/dual-mem fg;
+B: 1194/142/679/145), with no refusal. Text-only replay; image+spec remains untested.
+
+## 11. Prod arm selection (round 4)
+
+Per the item's rule (higher dual-agent greedy decode tok/s), **A** is chosen: 25.5 >
+23.0, and the same with length rows excluded (26.1 > 23.0). Caveats for the next
+decision: A is below off on dual-agent (25.5/26.1 vs 26.3), flat on combined (52.6 vs
+52.5), and induces 4 spec-driven loops; B is worse in every dual metric. Next runs: 
+`off/prod`, then `A/prod`. Deploy A to the live stack only if prod sampling shows a
+both-slots gain; otherwise leave the stack alone (milestone criterion, §1).
